  "body": {
    "id": "thm:local-constructive-completeness",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(S_t=\\varnothing\\) for \\(t\\ne k\\) and\n\\(S_k\\subseteq\\{k-1,k,k+1\\}\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,T\\}\\).  Then\n\\[\n\\mathsf C_{1,\\mathrm{loc}}(T,k,S_k,B,(|\\mathcal X_t|)_t)=1\n\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n\\operatorname{GID}(T,S,B)=1.\n\\]\nEquivalently, purely lagged or empty substantive parents of the sole possibly informative hazard require no audit, whereas a current or lead parent requires some pre-\\(k\\) dropout stratum to audit a coordinate at or downstream of \\(j_\\star=\\max(S_k\\cap\\{k,k+1\\})\\).  On success the procedure returns an evaluable simultaneous reconstruction of the entire vector \\((Q_a(x))_{a,x}\\); on failure it returns a legal strictly positive observationally equivalent pair with different endpoint vectors.  The equivalence is rank-free and allows null effects on every allowed arrow.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "T",
